    "reading": "Resident memory climbs about 6 MB in the first thirty seconds and then oscillates inside a 1.16 MB band for the remaining fourteen and a half minutes, while descriptors do not grow at all. That rules out the fast failures this is aimed at: a handle opened per request, or memory that climbs without returning. It does not rule out a slow leak. The least-squares slope over the settled window is +794 kB/hour, which is small against a 1.16 MB oscillation band and therefore indistinguishable from noise *at this duration* -- fourteen minutes cannot separate a 794 kB/hour trend from the sawtooth of a garbage-collected runtime. Saying it is noise would be a claim this run does not support; the honest statement is that a longer soak is what would settle it.",
